11
00:45:26,086 --> 00:45:32,086
Paddington is a 2014 live-action animated comedy film
written and directed by Paul King.

12
00:49:33,913 --> 00:49:39,913
It was developed from a story by King and Hamish McColl, which was based on the
stories of the character Paddington Bear created by Michael Bond.

13
00:53:41,739 --> 00:53:47,739
Produced by David Heyman, Paddington stars Ben Whishaw as the voice of the title character, with Hugh Bonneville,
Sally Hawkins, Julie Walters, Jim Broadbent, Peter Capaldi, and Nicole Kidman in live-action roles.

14
00:57:49,565 --> 00:57:55,565
The film tells the story of Paddington, an anthropomorphic bear who migrates from the jungles of "Darkest Peru" to the
streets of London, where he is adopted by the Brown family, unaware he is being pursued by a taxidermist.

15
01:01:57,391 --> 01:02:03,391
A British and French venture produced by StudioCanal UK, Heyday Films, TF1 Films Production and Anton Capital
Entertainment, Paddington's principal photography began in September 2013 and wrapped up in June 2014.

16
01:06:05,217 --> 01:06:11,217
Colin Firth was originally set to voice Paddington, but dropped
out in post-production and was replaced by Whishaw.

17
01:10:13,043 --> 01:10:19,043
Paddington was released in the United Kingdom on 28
November 2014 and in France on 3 December.

18
01:14:20,869 --> 01:14:26,869
The film received critical acclaim, and grossed $326
million against a €38.5 million budget.

19
01:18:28,695 --> 01:18:34,695
It received two nominations at the BAFTAs: Best
British Film and Best Adapted Screenplay.

20
01:22:36,521 --> 01:22:42,521
A sequel, Paddington 2, was released in 2017, and a further
sequel, Paddington in Peru, was released in 2024.

21
01:26:44,347 --> 01:26:50,347
The film explores themes of london, england, based on
novel or book, peru, anthropomorphism, bear.

22
01:30:52,173 --> 01:30:58,173
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and intense.
